 "text": "Hey, how are you holding up? That's a dead end. Let's find fresh way. How's reading comics these days? It is, but it' also the most fun way. Pick book you' always meant to read, but never found the motivation for. Start at beginning and read it cover to cover. It is, but only in the same way as binge watching a series. You' spending time with one character and one story, and that's nice. A language teacher or a tutor who knows the system? They'd spot it straight away and show you how to fix it. Great idea. Journals are wonderful for building confidence too. You don't have to show it to anyone, and little you write, the little you learn.",
